    "title_en": "Search for the $^{16}\\text{O}(ppp) \\rightarrow ^{13}\\text{C} π^+ π^+ e^+$ Decay Mode in Super-Kamiokande Using Machine Learning Techniques",
    "abstract_en": "We report a new partial lifetime limit of $4.2 \\times 10^{32}$ years for the trinucleon decay mode $^{16}\\text{O}(ppp) \\rightarrow ^{13}\\text{C} π^+ π^+ e^+$, obtained from a search conducted using the Super-Kamiokande detector with 0.401 megaton-years of exposure across five operational periods (SK-I: 1996--2001, SK-II: 2002--2005, SK-III: 2006--2008, SK-IV: 2008--2018, SK-V: 2019--2020). This represents an improvement of six orders of magnitude over previous experimental constraints. The analysis utilizes a convolutional neural network (CNN) incorporating an attention mechanism---a computational technique that enables the model to focus on the most relevant regions of Cherenkov ring patterns---to enhance event classification, thereby improving the sensitivity of the search. This is the first application of a CNN to a nucleon decay search in Super-Kamiokande. Furthermore, the large dataset available in Super-Kamiokande (hereafter \"SK\") strengthens the statistical power of the study, enabling a more stringent constraint than those set by prior experiments.",
